\section{End-to-End Workflow}
The input data are first selected through the rule-based GUI. The application
identifies the PRI associated with the selected Beam file and obtains the
relevant wake information from the PRI Analysis file. The specified
processing logic is applied and a labelled output is generated.

For model development, Beam signal data and corresponding labels are prepared
as supervised-learning examples. The training pipeline converts each channel
signal into a spectrogram representation and trains the classification model.
The saved model is then loaded by the prediction GUI to process new Beam data.

\chapter{Rule-Based Wake Signal Processing GUI}
\section{Purpose}
The first GUI provides an interface for processing the input datasets using
predefined rules. It reduces repeated manual file handling and organises the
generated channel-wise labels into a structured output.

\section{Input Data}
\subsection{Beam PRI CSV}
The Beam file contains signal observations arranged in channel columns. The
data format may represent each channel using an I/Q pair. The processing
pipeline identifies the I-channel values and excludes the corresponding
Q-channel values when the selected processing rule requires I-only input.

\subsection{PRI Analysis CSV}
The PRI Analysis file contains PRI-related information and the
Wake Detection field, along with other analysis fields. The PRI number is
used to associate a Beam file with the corresponding analysis record.

\section{PRI Matching and Label Generation}
The application obtains the PRI identifier from the Beam filename or the
selected file's metadata, according to the dataset naming convention. It
then locates the corresponding PRI record in the Analysis CSV. The wake
label is generated using the agreed Wake Detection interpretation.

If Wake Detection is encoded as a hexadecimal bit mask, the exact mapping
between bit positions and channel numbers must be verified against the
dataset specification or confirmed labelled examples. A bit order must not
be assumed without verification.

\section{Output}
The rule-based GUI saves a labelled PRI output file. The output is intended
to retain the channel-wise organisation required by the project. The first
valid observation of each I channel must be preserved during reading and
transformation. CSV header handling must be configured according to whether
the source file contains a header row.

