\chapter{Testing and Evaluation}
\section{Functional Testing}
Functional testing should verify:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
\item The GUI accepts valid Beam and PRI Analysis CSV files.
\item The PRI identifier is extracted and matched correctly.
\item I-channel extraction follows the actual column layout.
\item The first valid I-channel observation is preserved.
\item The rule-based output contains the expected channel labels.
\item The prediction GUI loads the saved model successfully.
\item Inference uses the same preprocessing as training.
\item Prediction output is saved to the selected location.
\item Invalid or mismatched files produce a clear error message.
\end{itemize}

\section{Model Evaluation}
The final report should present metrics computed on an independent test
set. Accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and confusion matrix are
recommended. Where appropriate, results should also be reported per
channel. Any performance values inserted into this chapter must come from
the actual final evaluation run.

\section{Limitations}
Model reliability depends on the quality and quantity of labelled data,
the correctness of the Wake\_Detection interpretation, preprocessing
consistency, and the representativeness of the training data. A
spectrogram-based image classifier may not preserve all aspects of the
original raw signal. Predictions must be validated against independent
labelled recordings before being used as evidence of operational detection
performance.

\chapter{Windows Packaging and Deployment}
\section{Packaging}
The prediction GUI can be packaged using PyInstaller. The deployment
package must include the GUI application, required runtime libraries,
the trained model, and any preprocessing configuration files needed
at inference time.

A directory-based PyInstaller build contains an executable and supporting
files. The complete generated application directory must be transferred;
copying only the executable may prevent the application from starting.

\section{Running on Another Windows Computer}
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
\item Build and test the application on the development computer.
\item Locate the generated application directory.
\item Copy the complete directory, including its internal dependency
folder and model resources.
\item Transfer it to a compatible Windows computer using an approved
transfer method.
\item Run the application executable and test it with a suitable Beam
input file.
\end{enumerate}
A separate Python installation is generally not required on the target
computer when the application has been packaged correctly. The final
package should nevertheless be tested on the intended Windows environment.

