\chapter{Conclusion and Future Work}
\section{Conclusion}
This project develops a structured workflow for sonar ship-wake data
processing and channel-wise prediction. The rule-based PySide6 GUI provides
file selection, PRI association, application of the specified labelling
rules, and generation of labelled output. The deep-learning workflow
prepares channel signal data, generates spectrogram representations, and
trains an EfficientNet-B0-based binary classification model using
TensorFlow and Keras. A separate prediction GUI can load the saved model
and apply it to new Beam data.

The project combines desktop application development, CSV data handling,
signal preprocessing, supervised learning, model saving, inference, and
Windows packaging. The final reliability of the prediction component must
be established through independent testing and verification of the
channel-label mapping.

\section{Future Work}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
\item Verify the hexadecimal Wake\_Detection bit mapping using authoritative
dataset documentation and known labelled examples.
\item Expand and diversify the labelled training dataset.
\item Introduce recording-wise or acquisition-wise validation and testing
to avoid data leakage.
\item Compare EfficientNet-B0 with signal-native one-dimensional CNN
architectures and other suitable models.
\item Investigate class imbalance, threshold selection, and per-channel
performance.
\item Improve preprocessing for variable-length signal sequences while
preserving all valid observations.
\item Add model version information and preprocessing metadata to the
deployed application.
\item Conduct further testing on independent sonar recordings.
\end{itemize}

